    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d155">

                <pb facs="0397" n="369" sameAs="frus:frus1955-57v26/pg369"/>

                <head>155. Telegram From the Department of State to the
                        Embassy in France<anchor n="1" xml:id="d155-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1955-05-09T17:52:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 9,
                                1955—5:52 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Tosec 7. For Merchant<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d155-f2"/> from Elbrick. We
                    are proceeding Washington approach British and French re possible use force
                    contemplated NSC 5404/1,<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d155-f3"/> which was deferred pending ratification Paris Agreements.
                    Will use current Autobahn situation as introduction (re Secto 2, rptd Bonn 846, London 1110).<anchor
                        n="4" xml:id="d155-f4"/></p>
                <p>Meanwhile, we hopeful dispatch instructions Bonn today re Autobahn situation
                    which envisage Allied and German planning in event approaches Soviets
                    unproductive. This would include use military facilities for which we are
                    seeking Defense approval.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">Hoover</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d155-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d155-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Central Files, 962A.7162B/5–855. Secret. Drafted by
                    Blumberg, cleared with Lyon, and approved
                    by Elbrick. Repeated to Bonn and
                    London.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d155-f2" n="2" xml:id="d155-f2-content">
                <p>Merchant was in Paris for the meeting of
                    the North Atlantic Council, May 9–11.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d155-f3" n="3" xml:id="d155-f3-content">
                <p>See <ref target="frus1952-54v07p2#pg_1390"><hi rendition="#italic">Foreign
                            Relations,</hi>, 1952–1954, vol. VII, Part 2, p. 1390</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d155-f4" n="4" xml:id="d155-f4-content">
                <p>Secto 2 reported that
                        Dulles had approved an approach to the British and
                    French with regard to Berlin. (Department of State, Central Files,
                    962A.7162A/5–855)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
